t the focus is on the second DLC to  complete and finish the story there will  be two new bosses and we've actually  seen all elements of both of the fights  in what is presumably the main boss  fight the female character clearly  serves as phase one displaying this  dominance over the tied up all-father as  to the woman's identity she's actually  been mentioned in game already the core  vien great scythe reads the mistress of  the painted world is said to wield a  great scythe herself and we always  assumed that this was referring to  Priscilla of Dark Souls 1 but since the  word mistress actually means a woman in  position of authority or control it's  clearly in my opinion referring to this  woman someone with a thematic connection  to Priscilla with the core viens and  with the way of white also perhaps this  woman is Lloyd's apostle mentioned in  the white sands ring description perhaps  she's Gertrude a woman described as a  heretic which might explain the source  of the heretical stories the winged core  viens tell or throughout the land or  perhaps she's as yet unnamed I read that  there were a lot of people crying velka  as soon as they saw her and honestly I'd  be a bit disappointed if this was Velka  I don't envision Velka this god that the  other gods and Lords fear I don't  envision her as a simple humanoid being  to be honest the other boss fight starts  with a human duel as well with the wolf  joining the fight after the defender  falls according to polygon but  interestingly in the trailer we don't  see the wolf join the fight after the  death of the human we see him join  immediately after this shield bash so  why is that why is there a discrepancy  in the information here my best guess is  that the flash of the wolf's face here  when you get shield bashed might trigger  the wolf's appearance  in the fight early if you get caught by  it and considering that this human enemy  is so oddly dressed and actually a  player like NPC do you think this could  be a sign that this is an actual player  like in the mirror night fight from Dark  Souls 2 for example I hope so that was  one of the best encounters in Dark Souls  2 and I love the way the wolf fights I  just have to say that it's so  reminiscent of SIF and I do believe it  is SIF or at least it's an incarnation  of him just like Osiris was an  incarnation of safe for example the  visual details are identical his face  and his eyes are exactly the same I  can't wait to find out more about why he  is here and I do hope they really  fleshed out this part of the story  because they run the risk of this just  being a shallow throwback if they don't  flesh it out anyway my favorite move of  his is this one where he misses you to  kick up all the snow and then he attacks  you from within the mist it's this  fighting style that's consistent with  how the wolves are described in game as  enemies how they can found their prey  when they fight and regularly sized  wolves are enemies in the DLC too though  we only see one in the trailer he's  hidden at the back here polygon  describes them as devious they say they  watch from a distance and they maintain  that distance until the entire pack is  gathered and only then will they all  attack at once and I like that I think  it's really important for the designers  of this DLC to keep the player's mind  occupied with visual elements like the  Wolves constantly threatening you that's  a great one because in open level design  like this it's easy to get a bit bored  because you don't quite need the same  awareness you do when you're traversing  a complex dungeon and it's traps other  enemies include these tree women which  I'm guessing are which trees as the  witch tree stave item description says  that their customary in the far north  and we know that the north is a cold  place from the  northern said and there are enemies  wearing very northern set esque armor  anyway regardless of what they're called  these long-limbed trees 